WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.302
-Tiffany,
you're a great comedian,

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.503
and part of your job is
to have strong opinions

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.871
about all different
kinds of things.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.372
So with that in mind,
I want to play a game

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:08.508
of "Wheel of Opinions."

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:13.746
♪ -Wheel of opinions ♪

00:00:13.746 --> 00:00:15.214
-Here's how this works.

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:16.482
I'm going to hit this button,

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:19.151
which will activate
the opinion-topic generator.

00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:20.687
It will land on a random topic.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:22.855
Whatever it is, you have to give
an opinion on it.

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:25.625
Ready for this?
-She ready.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.260
-I just wanted to
hear you say that.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.962
Here we go.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.470 line:0%
TikTok challenge.
TikTok challenges.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.806 line:0%
-Now, let me tell you, I'm here
for a good TikTok challenge.

00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:45.244 line:0%
I love to see people
take on dance routines,

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:48.848 line:0%
pranking their parents,
fun things like that.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.382 line:0%
I love a good TikTok challenge.

00:00:50.382 --> 00:00:53.953 line:0%
Just not doing it myself.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:57.023 line:0%
But sometimes I do,
but I prefer not to.

00:00:57.023 --> 00:01:00.626 line:0%
-By yourself, it's a no-go,
it's just bad?

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:03.262 line:0%
-Yeah, 'cause I, like, get
the dance routine down.

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:05.632 line:0%
It takes me two hours
to learn the routine.

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:08.034 line:0%
Then I get it down,
then I see myself doing it,

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:10.503 line:0%
and I'm like, "Nah, I'm good."

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.771 line:0%
So I only like to do
TikTok challenges

00:01:12.771 --> 00:01:16.642 line:0%
with my nieces or nephews,
something like that.

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:18.244 line:0%
With younger people
'cause I feel like

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.512 line:0%
I might be too old for it.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.648 line:0%
-Gotcha. Let's get to
another topic here.

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:29.589 line:0%
Okay, cats versus dogs.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:31.190 line:0%
-Okay, here goes the thing.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.259 line:0%
I got two dogs and I got a cat.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.361 line:0%
The cat from the movie "Keanu"
that I was in.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:38.731 line:0%
She lives with me and I'm pretty
sure she thinks she's a dog.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.033 line:0%
Cats are bossy.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.567 line:0%
Cats don't no play no games.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:45.538 line:0%
Dogs love to play games and dogs
love to follow directions.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.907 line:0%
-Yeah.
-So cats win.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.642 line:0%
Dogs follow.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:52.478 line:0%
-Oh, wow.

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:54.347 line:0%
-And that's why I love me.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.148 line:0%
-Wow, "that's why I love me."

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:57.417 line:0%
Oh, my gosh, interesting.

00:01:57.417 --> 00:02:00.987 line:0%
So it's possible you're
a cat and a dog person?

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:03.556 line:0%
-I'm both. I'm both.
-Wow, that's amazing.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.158 line:0%
-I'm both.
-Alright. Here we go.

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.531 line:0%
Surprise albums.

00:02:12.531 --> 00:02:15.435 line:0%
Everyone's dropping
a surprise album.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:19.272 line:0%
-I mean, I got like three
surprise albums out there,

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:21.975 line:0%
but I don't even know if anybody
know about the surprise.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:26.812 line:0%
I suggest y'all go to iTunes and
Apple and check out your girl.

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:28.647 line:0%
You know,
I'm on Spotify and all that.

00:02:28.647 --> 00:02:31.651 line:0%
I got a song called
"Come and Get Your Baby Daddy."

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:34.887 line:0%
Got another song called
"I Got a Man."

00:02:34.887 --> 00:02:37.690 line:0%
Got another song -- I got
a bunch of songs out, actually.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:38.824 line:0%
Check me out.

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:40.993 line:0%
-Too many surprises.
Too many surprises.

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:43.162 line:0%
I love it.
Alright, here we go.

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:44.764 line:0%
Final topic.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.369 line:0%
Psychedelic tea.

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:52.738 line:0%
I'm assuming like mushroom tea
or one of these things.

00:02:52.738 --> 00:02:55.508 line:0%
-Okay, let me tell you something
about mushroom tea, okay?

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:56.943 line:0%
It is not my thing.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:03:00.346 line:0%
Okay, so I went to
Dave Chappelle's, right?

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.614 line:0%
To do some comedy.

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.649 line:0%
I got peer-pressured into
drinking the tea.

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:05.384 line:0%
Now, I'm gonna tell you.
I don't do drugs.

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:07.753 line:0%
It's not my thing.
I don't do drugs.

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:09.454 line:0%
But I said,
"Okay, I'm gonna drink this tea

00:03:09.454 --> 00:03:11.023 line:0%
since everybody else is."

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:12.325 line:0%
And I drank it.

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.826 line:0%
And Jon Hamm was there.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.396 line:0%
And as Jon Hamm is talking,

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:19.299 line:0%
he started to look like
Phylicia Rashad.

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:20.800 line:0%
And as I started looking around,

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.202 line:0%
everybody started looking like
Phylicia Rashad.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:25.304 line:0%
The black people,
the white people.

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:27.473 line:0%
Dave Chappelle looked like
Phylicia Rashad,

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:30.209
bald-headed with pointy ears.

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:33.079
I think I had to go to therapy.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:34.814
I went to my therapist.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.482
That's a weird trip.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.818
-A Phylicia Rashad issue,
and I think it's because

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:41.120
I really want Phylicia Rashad
to be my mama.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.955
-Yes, we all do.

00:03:42.955 --> 00:03:46.191
-I'm gonna have to write a movie
and cast her in it to be my mom.

00:03:46.191 --> 00:03:48.027
That's what I gathered from
that, and I will no longer.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.662
-That is trippy.
Alright, you win.

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.364
You win the night.
You are the best.

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.832
Thank you for playing
"Wheel of Opinions."

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:55.067
My thanks again to
the great Tiffany Haddish.

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:56.836
Congrats again on the Emmy nom!

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.204
We miss you.
Hope to see you in person.

00:03:58.204 --> 00:03:59.272
-Thank you.
-Bye, bud.

